sec.p:
The invasive growth of cholesteatoma and the associated destruction of bone structures in the middle ear is associated with inflammation and immunological processes and represent a considerable challenge in otology4,10,11. Given the delicate anatomy of the middle ear, particular attention must be paid to the small dimensions of the structures that need to be preserved. The stapes typically measures \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
